      "writtenOn": "2025-04-18T22:55:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"D3D12RobustnessTransformIgnoreNoBuffer\" is confusingly named to me, specifically the \"ignore no buffer\" part. Are we saying that we need to have robustness checks for all buffers on QC hardware, unconditionally?  If so, should rename to be \"ForceRobustnessCheckForAllBuffers\", or something like that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 309,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "36ba3c8a42240b32482e4714ab651c86e0919ddf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6e199ad_01e1998f",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/ShaderModuleD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000262
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-18T22:55:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To clarify, buffers bound in the root signature do NOT have out of bounds checking. [SetGraphicsRootUnorderedAccessView](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/nf-d3d12-id3d12graphicscommandlist-setgraphicsrootunorderedaccessview) and [SetGraphicsRootConstantBufferView](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/nf-d3d12-id3d12graphicscommandlist-setgraphicsrootconstantbufferview) just accept a root parameter index and a GPU virtual address. Since no \"size\" or \"count of elements\" is passed in, the driver/hardware is not able to do bounds checking.\n\n[CreateUnorderedAccessView](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/nf-d3d12-id3d12device-createunorderedaccessview) and [CreateConstantBufferView](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/nf-d3d12-id3d12device-createconstantbufferview), on the other hand, accept a \"size in bytes\" parameter so the hardware/driver is able to do bounds checking.",
      "parentUuid": "8584b7eb_8380eb6d",
      "revId": "36ba3c8a42240b32482e4714ab651c86e0919ddf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9392709a_6f12d842",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/ShaderModuleD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-21T09:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We also [don\u0027t set the flag](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d12/PipelineLayoutD3D12.cpp;drc\u003de8e3490269a003ae1f1e92c9ae0ae30cdbdd3de0;l\u003d238) on the root signature that will cause the OOB checks to be skipped.",
      "parentUuid": "f6e199ad_01e1998f",
      "revId": "36ba3c8a42240b32482e4714ab651c86e0919ddf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd3faf37_f2ede196",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/ShaderModuleD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-21T10:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e To clarify, buffers bound in the root signature do NOT have out of bounds checking. SetGraphicsRootUnorderedAccessView and SetGraphicsRootConstantBufferView just accept a root parameter index and a GPU virtual address.\n\nYes, but if I get it right Dawn [use descriptor table for non-dynamic-binding-offset buffer](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d12/PipelineLayoutD3D12.cpp;l\u003d206;drc\u003d5e01cdc5efe08fe9bedf7cc1523b8094b626559d?q\u003dDATA_VOLATILE\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fdawn%2Fsrc%2F) instead of directly bound them in the root signature. Only dynamic binding buffers are [directly bound to root signature without using descriptor table](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d12/PipelineLayoutD3D12.cpp;l\u003d256;drc\u003d5e01cdc5efe08fe9bedf7cc1523b8094b626559d?q\u003dDATA_VOLATILE\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fdawn%2Fsrc%2F), and currently we always do index clamping for these DBO buffers.\n\nAnd I concerned that if root signature 1.1 might allow skipping OOB checks by default (as opposite to root signature 1.0) if [DESCRIPTORS_VOLATILE is not set](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d12/root-signature-version-1-1#:~:text\u003dIf%20applications%20depend%20on%20safe%20out%20of%20bounds%20memory%20access%20behavior%20when%20accessing%20descriptors%2C%20they%20need%20to%20mark%20the%20descriptor%20ranges%20that%20access%20those%20descriptors%20as%20DESCRIPTORS_VOLATILE.), as I pasted in the [issue](https://issues.chromium.org/issues/410985021).",
      "parentUuid": "9392709a_6f12d842",
      "revId": "36ba3c8a42240b32482e4714ab651c86e0919ddf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
